WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.707
Real rules often have more than one condition.

2
00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:08.795
In this lesson, you will learn to combine conditions with OR, fix a common

3
00:00:08.795 --> 00:00:13.156
type error, and check your new column with filters, row by row.

4
00:00:13.156 --> 00:00:15.700
Let's make sure our logic is right!

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:25.120
In Table view, I click New column, and name it SP01 and SP02 Cancelled. The goal:

6
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.940
flag cancelled orders for two salespeople.

7
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.763
I type IF, then OR.

8
00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:45.418
The tooltip says OR returns true if any of its arguments are true, and

9
00:00:45.418 --> 00:00:47.080
false if all are false.

10
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.353
The first condition:

11
00:01:03.353 --> 00:01:05.024
Order Status equals Cancelled.

12
00:01:05.024 --> 00:01:09.620
Then a comma, and the second condition about the salesperson ID.

13
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.439
I add the results:

14
00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:45.447
Ask the reason, or Leave it.

15
00:01:45.447 --> 00:01:47.120
But the column shows errors.

16
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.257
The message says:

17
00:01:53.257 --> 00:01:57.887
cannot convert value SP02 of type text to type true or false.

18
00:01:57.887 --> 00:02:04.059
Here the second ID was written as text on its own, not as a full test.

19
00:02:04.059 --> 00:02:06.760
Every condition must be a complete comparison.

20
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.162
After the fix, the column works:

21
00:02:19.162 --> 00:02:20.880
Leave it for most rows.

22
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.255
Now let's check.

23
00:02:30.255 --> 00:02:35.645
I filter the salesperson column to one ID, and the order status to Cancelled.

24
00:02:35.645 --> 00:02:38.340
Every row shows Ask the reason. Correct!

25
00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.721
Then I filter Order Status to Delivered.

26
00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:51.968
Now every row shows Leave it.

27
00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.840
The logic works both ways.

28
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.220
Always test a new column with filters before you use it in a report. Trust, but verify!

